invariant: INV-16
file: record.c
catches: hash_runtime_test
reason: rec_dir_init_suite derives a direction's key under a value with
  every bit set, where it must hand on the direction's own cpu, which the
  session wrote from its ch_cfg.cpu. Every record direction of a session
  without CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 then derives its key from the
  traffic secret on SHA-256 instructions the caller never stated
  (docs/decisions.md 93). The key is the same. bin/hash_runtime_test keys
  a direction under each ch_cfg.cpu value and counts the calls into each
  path.

--- old
    HKDF_EXPAND_LABEL_CPU(d->cpu, hash_len, secret, "key", NULL, 0, d->key, suite_key_len(suite));
--- new
    HKDF_EXPAND_LABEL_CPU(~0U, hash_len, secret, "key", NULL, 0, d->key, suite_key_len(suite));
